# 📝 Building a To-Do List App with JavaScript

Here's a complete, beginner-friendly To-Do List app using plain **HTML, CSS, and JavaScript** — no frameworks needed!

---

## 1. HTML (`index.html`)

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>To-Do List</title>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="style.css">
</head>
<body>
  <div class="container">
    <h1>📝 My To-Do List</h1>
    <div class="input-group">
      <input type="text" id="taskInput" placeholder="Add a new task..." />
      <button id="addBtn">Add</button>
    </div>
    <ul id="taskList"></ul>
    <p class="counter"><span id="taskCount">0</span> tasks remaining</p>
  </div>
  <script src="app.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
```

---

## 2. CSS (`style.css`)

```css
* { margin: 0; padding: 0; box-sizing: border-box; }

body {
  font-family: 'Segoe UI', sans-serif;
  background: #f0f4f8;
  display: flex;
  justify-content: center;
  padding-top: 60px;
}

.container {
  background: #fff;
  padding: 30px;
  border-radius: 12px;
  box-shadow: 0 4px 20px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);
  width: 400px;
}

h1 { text-align: center; margin-bottom: 20px; color: #333; }

.input-group { display: flex; gap: 8px; margin-bottom: 20px; }

#taskInput {
  flex: 1;
  padding: 10px 14px;
  border: 2px solid #ddd;
  border-radius: 8px;
  font-size: 16px;
  outline: none;
}
#taskInput:focus { border-color: #4a90d9; }

#addBtn {
  padding: 10px 20px;
  background: #4a90d9;
  color: #fff;
  border: none;
  border-radius: 8px;
  font-size: 16px;
  cursor: pointer;
}
#addBtn:hover { background: #357abd; }

ul { list-style: none; }

li {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: space-between;
  padding: 12px;
  border-bottom: 1px solid #eee;
  font-size: 16px;
}

li.completed span { text-decoration: line-through; color: #aaa; }

li button {
  background: #e74c3c;
  color: white;
  border: none;
  border-radius: 6px;
  padding: 4px 10px;
  cursor: pointer;
}

.counter { text-align: center; margin-top: 16px; color: #888; }
```

---

## 3. JavaScript (`app.js`)

```javascript
// --- DOM Elements ---
const taskInput = document.getElementById('taskInput');
const addBtn    = document.getElementById('addBtn');
const taskList  = document.getElementById('taskList');
const taskCount = document.getElementById('taskCount');

// --- Load tasks from localStorage ---
let tasks = JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem('tasks')) || [];

// --- Render all tasks ---
function renderTasks() {
  taskList.innerHTML = '';

  tasks.forEach((task, index) => {
    const li = document.createElement('li');
    if (task.completed) li.classList.add('completed');

    li.innerHTML = `
      <span>${task.text}</span>
      <div>
        <button onclick="toggleTask(${index})">✔</button>
        <button onclick="deleteTask(${index})">✖</button>
      </div>
    `;
    taskList.appendChild(li);
  });

  // Update remaining count
  const remaining = tasks.filter(t => !t.completed).length;
  taskCount.textContent = remaining;

  // Save to localStorage
  localStorage.setItem('tasks', JSON.stringify(tasks));
}

// --- Add a new task ---
function addTask() {
  const text = taskInput.value.trim();
  if (text === '') return;

  tasks.push({ text, completed: false });
  taskInput.value = '';
  renderTasks();
}

// --- Toggle complete/incomplete ---
function toggleTask(index) {
  tasks[index].completed = !tasks[index].completed;
  renderTasks();
}

// --- Delete a task ---
function deleteTask(index) {
  tasks.splice(index, 1);
  renderTasks();
}

// --- Event Listeners ---
addBtn.addEventListener('click', addTask);
taskInput.addEventListener('keypress', (e) => {
  if (e.key === 'Enter') addTask();
});

// --- Initial render ---
renderTasks();
```

---

## ✨ Key Features

| Feature | How it works |
|---|---|
| **Add tasks** | Type + click "Add" or press Enter |
| **Complete tasks** | Click ✔ to toggle strikethrough |
| **Delete tasks** | Click ✖ to remove |
| **Persistence** | Tasks saved in `localStorage` — survives page refresh |
| **Task counter** | Shows remaining incomplete tasks |

---

## 🚀 Ideas to Extend It

- **Edit tasks** — double-click a task to rename it
- **Filter view** — buttons for All / Active / Completed
- **Due dates** — add a date picker and sort by deadline
- **Drag & drop** — reorder tasks by dragging
- **Categories/tags** — group tasks by project or priority
- **Use a framework** — rebuild with React, Vue, or Svelte for practice

Just save the three files in the same folder, open `index.html` in your browser, and you're good to go!

